{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9meR8DNoYcC13EKqV1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A `save_fact` should now re-cache only the new fact (about 15 tokens) instead of the whole ~1050-token prompt. I haven't run it against the real API: there's no key here and the SDK isn't installed.\n\n**What was going wrong:** the system prompt was one cached block containing the instructions, profile, facts and date. In `logs/usage.jsonl`, the full re-cache doesn't land on the next message. It lands on the second round of the same message's tool loop: `reply()` adds the fact to the athlete record in place, so the very next call rebuilds the prompt with it. The date line was in that block too, which caused a second full re-cache once a day per athlete.\n\n**The change, in `build_system()` in `bot.py`:** the system prompt is now a list of blocks.\n1. **Instructions and the profile that rarely changes** (name, sport, zones, goal, language), with a cache marker. Nothing in it changes per day or per message.\n2. **One block per fact**, in the order saved, with a cache marker on the last one. Since `save_fact` only adds to the end, the prompt cached by the previous call is still the exact start of the new one. The API checks earlier block boundaries for a match, so it reads that from cache and only writes the new fact.\n3. **`Today:` after the last marker**, so it's never cached and a new day doesn't invalidate anything.\n\nThe prompt text changed slightly: \"(none yet)\" is gone (replacing it on the first save would have broken the match) and `Language:` moved above the facts.\n\n**Checks:** I added `tests/test_cache_layout.py`, which runs offline against a fake client that follows Anthropic's documented caching rules. It checks that a `save_fact` re-caches less than 5% of the prompt, a new day re-caches nothing, and the instructions block stays identical. All 3 tests pass on the new code and all 3 fail on the original. Its token counts are a characters-divided-by-4 estimate, not real numbers. To confirm live, trigger a `save_fact` and look at the next round's usage: `cache_creation_input_tokens` should be about one fact's size.\n\n**What applied from the colleague's note** (the full breakdown is in `ANSWER.md`):\n- **Applied:** splitting stable instructions from the changing part, two markers, keeping dates out of the stable part, loading all facts rather than a per-message selection, and reading `usage` to find the miss.\n- **Probably wouldn't have worked here alone:** their two-marker split. Sonnet 4.5 won't cache anything shorter than 1024 tokens, and this bot's tools plus instructions come to roughly 950–1000. The marker after the instructions may never create a cache entry, so every fact would still re-cache the full prompt. The one-block-per-fact layout avoids that limit. I kept the instructions marker anyway because it's harmless.\n- **Left alone:** tool filtering, which NOTES.md says to keep. A message that pulls in the planning or race tools still re-caches the whole prompt once, because the tool list sits before the system prompt in what gets cached.\n\nThis depends on facts only ever being added. If editing or deleting facts is ever added, everything after the changed fact will be re-cached.\n\nNothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2236,"cache_read_input_tokens":39062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2236},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd07c743-fd69-4c9a-820c-f4671b47c3df","uuid":"386eae1a-fbee-45d6-b5de-3c6115a9ad64","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:59:56.897Z","request_id":"req_011CgS9meAFPGrnwSiATuioC"}
